cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this model in published work, please cite it, bandsolver, the papers it is based on
  (see README), and Newman's description of the BAND method (Electrochemical Systems, Appendix C).
title: "znmno2-model: an aqueous Zn/MnO2 cell model with solution speciation, solved with Newman's BAND method"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: John
    family-names: Bernard
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/jcbernard87/znmno2-model"
abstract: >-
  A one-dimensional model of an aqueous Zn/MnO2 cell with dilute-solution transport, solution
  speciation (pH and complexes at every point), MnO2 dissolution and deposition, Zn insertion and
  zinc hydroxide sulfate precipitation, solved by finite volumes, backward Euler and Newton's method
  with the BAND block-tridiagonal solver. The model versions of the original research are options.
keywords:
  - zinc-ion battery
  - MnO2
  - aqueous electrolyte
  - speciation
  - porous electrode
  - Newman
